From: Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>
Subject: Refresh the dependency lock past 22 advisories

Upstream's Cargo.lock dates from the 1.39.0 release and pins crate
versions that have since been fixed. Every change here is the
semver-compatible resolution cargo picks on its own, so no manifest
requirement moves; the companion patch handles zip, whose fix needed a
new major.

What this clears, with the version the lock reaches:

 * quinn-proto 0.11.8 to 0.11.19: CVE-2026-31812, GHSA-4w2j-m93h-cj5j
 * rustls-webpki 0.102.8 to 0.103.16: GHSA-82j2-j2ch-gfr8,
   GHSA-pwjx-qhcg-rvj4, GHSA-965h-392x-2mh5, GHSA-xgp8-3hg3-c2mh
 * hashbrown 0.15.0 to 0.17.1: GHSA-wwq9-3cpr-mm53
 * rustls 0.23.16 to 0.23.46: GHSA-2mjx-qc3c-rqvc, GHSA-c8m5-c952-6cm4,
   GHSA-qg5g-gv98-5ffh, GHSA-h2v8-394m-p7vv, GHSA-w44r-93j7-qv28
 * tar 0.4.42 to 0.4.46: CVE-2026-33055, CVE-2026-33056,
   GHSA-3pv8-6f4r-ffg2
 * ring 0.17.8 to 0.17.14: CVE-2025-4432
 * idna 0.5.0 to 1.1.0, via url 2.5.0 to 2.5.8: CVE-2024-12224
 * time 0.3.36 to 0.3.55: CVE-2026-25727
 * bytes 1.8.0 to 1.12.1: CVE-2026-25541
 * tokio 1.41.0 to 1.54.1: GHSA-rr8g-9fpq-6wmg
 * rand 0.8.5 to 0.10.3: GHSA-cq8v-f236-94qc

tar and ring matter most for what fnm does: it extracts downloaded
Node.js tarballs and verifies the release server's certificate.

Upstream's own test suite passes against this lock, all 30 tests,
including the zip extraction test and the Node install tests that
download real releases.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-04

